   "text": "I read the structure as a VHL-type PROTAC: a VHL ligand joined through a spiro linker to a bicyclic-amine/aminopyridazine-phenol warhead. This is the SMILES I derived from the drawing.\n\n**Regions, left to right**\n- **Top:** a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl phenyl ring attached to a CH(CH3)\u2013NH group, which is an (S)-1-arylethylamide.\n- **Hydroxyproline:** a 4-hydroxypyrrolidine-2-carboxamide with a hashed OH at C4.\n- **Tert-leucine:** the proline nitrogen is acylated by a tert-leucine (C(CH3)3 on the alpha carbon) whose NH is acylated in turn.\n- **Spiro linker:** that acyl group is a carboxamide on a spiro[3.5]nonane. The cyclohexane carbon carries the carboxamide on a wedge, and the cyclobutane carbon carries the piperidine nitrogen on a hash.\n- **Piperidine\u2013pyrimidine:** the piperidine's 4-position is bonded to the 5-position of a pyrimidine.\n- **Bicyclic amine:** the pyrimidine's 2-position is bonded to the bridging nitrogen (N8) of a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. Its other nitrogen (N3) is bonded to the pyridazine.\n- **Pyridazine:** a 3-amino-pyridazine bearing a 2-hydroxyphenyl group.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- I assigned the spiro-ring centres from the wedge/hash geometry in the drawing.\n- The (S)-1-arylethylamine, the hydroxyproline and the tert-leucine centres are written as the standard VHL ligand configuration. I matched them against that known ligand rather than re-deriving each from the drawing.\n- The bicyclic amine is drawn without stereo, so it has none in the SMILES.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@@H]1C[C@@H](O)CN1C(=O)[C@@H](NC(=O)[C@H]2CCC3(CC2)C[C@@H](C3)N2CCC(CC2)c2cnc(nc2)N2C3CCC2CN(C3)c2cc(nnc2N)-c2ccccc2O)C(C)(C)C)c2ccc(-c3scnc3C)cc2"
